{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"MECHANISM CORRECTED before implementing — my scope note for the folded-in bug 5f48 was wrong, and the\ncorrection changes what the fix must do.\n\nI wrote that every inbound DC ghost-identity mint FAILS silently. It does not: the mint is never\nATTEMPTED. _ensure_inbound_assignee_identity (apply_inbound_records.py:50) returns early unless the\nassignee carries a non-empty accountId, and identity_model.py:26 states DC has no accountId at all —\nDC users carry name/key. It is called with the raw Jira user object (:155, :321), so the DC path exits\nat the guard.\n\nThat splits the work into TWO defects that COMPOUND:\n (a) ACTIVE: DC inbound assignees mint no identity at all — the guard demands an identifier DC never\n     supplies. Cloud gets ghost identities; DC silently does not. Nothing raises.\n (b) LATENT: the ValueError is real (proven at the API) but unreachable while the guard short-circuits.\n     It fires the moment someone teaches the guard DC's name — i.e. the moment someone fixes (a) ALONE.\n     And since the call sits in 'except Exception: # best-effort ghost mint' logged at DEBUG, that\n     one-line fix converts a silent no-op into a SWALLOWED EXCEPTION — strictly harder to diagnose.\n\nSo neither half alone is a fix, and the obvious fix to (a) makes things worse. Both land together.\nAdded an AC that pins exactly this: with the guard fixed but the channel unmapped, the mint raises and\nis swallowed. That test is what stops a future contributor from splitting them.\n\nHOW I CAUGHT IT: I was about to write the RED test and checked whether the DC path actually REACHES the\nfailing call, instead of assuming my API-level repro implied reachability. It did not. A repro proving\na function rejects an input says nothing about whether that input ever arrives — the same\ncheck-the-quantifier failure the handoff warned about, caught this time before it reached code.\n\nThe in-flight review-plan was killed rather than left to certify the wrong rationale; re-running."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785470150987678001,"uuid":"f65e244b-fa8d-4e72-9f57-240f0d12f2f1"}